atlas evidence-shell-static-audit

architecture shell-static-audit
  canonical_name ShellStaticAudit
  family evidence
  domain Evidence / Shell source analysis
  layer verification
  semantic_question Which discovered shell files did the installed ShellCheck analyze, which could it not analyze, and what exact source bytes were in scope?
  purpose Run one bounded read-only ShellCheck audit in ordinary CI with deterministic rg discovery, source hashes, complete diagnostics, and explicit unsupported-shell classification.
  maturity implemented
  source_path scripts/analysis/shellcheck_audit.mjs
  source_path scripts/tests/shellcheck_audit.test.mjs
  source_path .github/workflows/native-kernel.yml
  witness scripts/tests/shellcheck_audit.test.mjs covers actual-error refusal, missing-tool refusal, unsupported-shell separation, concurrent source-change refusal, and unknown-severity refusal; the installed 2026-10-02 ShellCheck 0.11.0 scan discovered 315 files, analyzed 314, reported one SC1071 unsupported file, zero other errors, and retained all warnings, info and style diagnostics
  invariant discovery names the exact existing source roots and globs and sorts paths bytewise; each input path and SHA-256 contributes to the reported scope digest
  invariant runner subprocesses have time and output limits; missing rg or ShellCheck, malformed output, unknown diagnostic severity, and input changes during the scan fail closed
  invariant SC1071 files are reported as unsupported and excluded from analyzed counts rather than suppressed, counted as errors, or called passed
  invariant all ShellCheck diagnostics, including warnings, info and style, remain in the JSON report; only actual non-SC1071 errors fail the source audit
  forbidden_inference no ShellCheck errors -> shell runtime correctness, safe deployment, absence of defects, or successful analysis of an unsupported shell
  known_gap ShellCheck cannot analyze scripts whose interpreter is outside its supported shell family; scripts/bonfyre_repo_inventory.sh remains explicitly unsupported, and the audit neither replaces runtime tests nor applies fixes

architecture javascript-static-audit
  canonical_name JavaScriptStaticAudit
  family evidence
  domain Evidence / Exact source analysis coverage
  layer verification
  maturity implemented
  semantic_question Did the requested JavaScript source bytes actually reach a real pinned analyzer, rather than merely produce a successful installer or wrapper exit?
  purpose Bind explicit source hashes, observed analyzer version, analyzed file and rule counts, diagnostics and process status into one fail-closed CI receipt.
  source_path scripts/analysis/oxlint_audit.mjs
  source_path scripts/tests/oxlint_audit.test.mjs
  source_path .github/workflows/native-kernel.yml
  witness scripts/tests/oxlint_audit.test.mjs covers missing or silent output, incomplete scope, changed source bytes, invalid diagnostics and executable/version refusal
  invariant every requested input is a bounded regular file beneath the audit root; duplicate paths and symlinks refuse
  invariant analyzer JSON must report the exact requested file count and a positive rule count; silent success and skipped input coverage fail
  invariant source identity and digest are checked before and after analysis; changed input invalidates the receipt
  invariant warnings remain visible and fail this explicit clean-source gate; malformed output or process status cannot be reclassified as success
  forbidden_inference zero analyzer diagnostics -> semantic correctness, security proof, runtime performance or analysis of any file outside the recorded scope
  known_gap the JavaScript gate checks an explicit scoped list; it is not a claim that all estate JavaScript is analyzed or clean

interaction javascript-audit-covers-project-mcp
  source javascript-static-audit
  destination mcp-project-native-owner
  relation source-bound-static-analysis
  preserves exact runtime, deployment and HTTP witness source paths, source digests, pinned analyzer version and observed coverage counts
  drops any inference from static analysis to live effect authority, deployment success or functional parity
  forbidden_inference a clean static-analysis receipt -> correctness of a native projection or safety of a production cutover
  binding .github/workflows/native-kernel.yml
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_node_cutover.json records explicit Oxlint JSON coverage separately from tests and deployment observations
